    {
      "id": "BEQ-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "A congruence lattice Riemann sum tends to the product of the local integrals",
      "anchor": "lifts-binary-equidistribution",
      "statement": "For m coordinates over a totally real field F of degree d, the sum over S-integers against continuous compactly supported real and S-local tests, multiplied by ε^(dm), tends to the product of their Haar integrals as ε tends to zero from above. In the inductive translated-ideal version the additional constant is N(I)^(−m).",
      "hypotheses": "S is finite, the real diagonal scaling comes from a continuous ring map ℝ→F∞, the standard real Haar measure gives the integers covolume one, and each local integer ring has volume one. In the inductive claim, I is a nonzero integral ideal coprime to the places under consideration.",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-binary-lattice-sum"
      ],
