      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "At the empty set of places use a tiling by translated ideal fundamental cells. At a new place approximate the continuous factor to precision u on disjoint residue boxes of radius 𝔭ᵏ. A congruence refinement identifies each restriction with one translated ideal of modulus I𝔭ᵏ and relative mass q^(−km). The finite approximation and the accompanying absolute-value sum both converge. The uniform bound on the combined volume of the boxes gives error O(u) after passing to their limits.",
      "review": "Verified the original finite-set induction, all measure normalizations, the absolute majorant and the translated ideal hypothesis against the pinned source."
