    {
      "id": "BEQ-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "Unitary translates of the vector count have a common integrable bound",
      "anchor": "lifts-binary-vector-limit",
      "statement": "In an anisotropic binary Hermitian space, the ε^(4d)-weighted genus integral over nonzero vectors tends to V, the ambient archimedean integral times the product of the exceptional finite coordinate volumes.",
      "hypotheses": "Use a nondegenerate Hermitian form on E² over a CM extension E/F, the standard Haar coordinate measures, a Haar measure on the unitary group and a fundamental domain of finite positive volume. The archimedean test is continuous, nonnegative and compactly supported on the regular Gram locus. The finitely many exceptional sets are compact open within the regular locus. The remaining sets are the standard vector lattices.",
