      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "Rewrite a fixed unitary translate with four F-coordinates and enlarge the exceptional set to include its finitely many nonintegral places. Local unitary transformations preserve the ambient Haar measures. A common finite denominator and compact real box dominate all the translates belonging to a compact set of representatives. A real continuous majorant and the lattice limit bound their scaled counts. Rational invariance and dominated convergence give the normalized average.",
      "review": "At F=ℚ, E=ℚ(i), J=I₂, the identity translate and the residue box (1,0,0,0) mod 3 with a regular product of real tents give exactly 135/8192 at N=4 and 1/81 whenever 3 divides N. The finite sums agree with the ordered-difference formula for all tested N."
