  "outstanding": [
    "The binary application assumes cocompactness with positive finite Haar quotient volume, Gram-fibre measures and their local mass estimates, and the local topology of the regular test. BSM supplies the common scalar on nonzero lengths. The regular local density formulas, the arithmetic construction of rational congruence representatives, and the general lattice scaling theorem are used in the component arguments. A numerical rate for the full scalar average is not supplied by this proof."
  ]
